    "description": "This dataset contains Water temperature, salinity, oxygen, currents and others taken by CTD, Niskin bottles, and ADCP from the research vessel Keifu Maru, cruise KS15-06, in the North Pacific Ocean. The entire cruise was carried out during the period from June to August, 2015. Hydrographic observation was made using a Sea-Bird Electronics (SBE) 36 position carousel equipped with 10-liter Niskin water sample bottles, a CTD system (SBE911plus) equipped with JFE Advantech oxygen sensor (RINKO III) along 165E. Water samples were analyzed for salinity, dissolved oxygen, nutrients, pH and phytopigment (chlorophyll-a and phaeopigments). Current data was measured by Teledyne RDI's vessel-mounted ADCP system\u00ef\u00bc\u008838kHz Ocean Surveyor\u00ef\u00bc\u0089.\n\nThis dataset is U.S. State Department MSR U2014-036 as part of the World Data Service for Oceanography\n\nData are in PDF.",
